1. Description

    Developed the Medicine Product Catalog for the Pharma Store website to provide customers with a structured and user-friendly interface for browsing available medicines and healthcare products.

    The catalog was designed to present important product information in a clear format, including product images, medicine names, pricing, availability, category information, and purchasing actions. The layout was optimized for both desktop and mobile users.

2. Business Requirement

    The Pharma Store required a dedicated product catalog where customers could easily:

     Browse available medicines.
     Identify products through images and names.
     View medicine pricing.
     Check product availability.
     Understand product categories.
     Add medicines to the shopping cart.
     Navigate from the catalog to individual product details.
     Browse products efficiently on different devices.

    The catalog also needed to provide a scalable foundation for future features such as search, filtering, sorting, subscriptions, offers, and personalized recommendations.

3. Features Implemented
    Product Listing

    Implemented a structured medicine product listing interface containing:

    Product image
    Product name
    Medicine type/category
    Price
    Discount information where applicable
    Availability status
    Add to Cart action
    View Product / product navigation
    Product Cards

    Created reusable product card components with a consistent layout.

    Each card provides:

    ┌──────────────────────────────┐
    │                              │
    │       Product Image          │
    │                              │
    ├──────────────────────────────┤
    │ Medicine Name                │
    │ Medicine Category            │
    │                              │
    │ ₹XXX                         │
    │                              │
    │ [ Add to Cart ]              │
    └──────────────────────────────┘

    The cards were designed to maintain consistent dimensions even when product names or images vary.

4. Product Image Integration

   Integrated healthcare product images into the catalog.

   Supported product visuals include:

   Medicine boxes
   Medicine bottles
   Tablets
   Capsules
   Blister packs
   Vitamins
   Supplements
   Healthcare products
   Medical devices

   Images were optimized to maintain consistent proportions within product cards.

5. Pricing Display

   Implemented a clear pricing hierarchy to make product costs easy to identify.

   Example:

   ₹499
   ₹399
   20% OFF

   Where applicable, the catalog can display:

   Original price
   Discounted price
   Discount percentage
   0Promotional pricing

6. Product Availability

   Added product availability indicators to help customers understand whether a medicine is currently available.

   Example statuses:

   In Stock
   Limited Stock
   Out of Stock

   The status is displayed using visually distinct UI indicators.

7. Add to Cart

   Integrated the Add to Cart action directly into the product card.

   The workflow allows users to:

   Select a product.
   Add the product to cart.
   Continue browsing.
   Review the cart later.
   Proceed toward checkout.

   This reduces unnecessary navigation and improves the shopping experience.

